{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_309441366#1_541138436","relevance":3,"reason":"Dedicated source on scopophobia, the fear of being watched or stared at, with a causes section directly explaining links to social/anxiety disorders, epilepsy/Tourette's, traumatic public ridicule, and visible physical differences.","learned":"Scopophobia can make people fear being watched or stared at; causes may include social anxiety, neurological conditions such as epilepsy or Tourette's, traumatic ridicule, or concerns about visible differences."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3762","reason":"This query is producing a highly relevant dedicated explanation of fear of being watched; continue to collect additional direct evidence from this source or related scopophobia sources."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3762"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_309441366#0_541136742","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3762","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_309441366#0_541136742\" , \"end_char\": 1191.000000 , \"headings\": \"Fear of Being Watched Phobia – Scopophobia Fear of Being Watched Phobia – Scopophobia Causes of Scopophobia Symptoms of fear of being watched Treating and overcoming Scopophobia \" , \"segment\": \"Fear of Being Watched Phobia - Scopophobia You are here: Home / Phobias / Fear of Being Watched Phobia – Scopophobia Fear of Being Watched Phobia – Scopophobia By Jacob Olesen 57 Comments<cover>Scopophobia or Scoptophobia is the fear of being watched or stared </cover>at. It originates from the Greek word ‘ skopein’ which means “to look or to examine” and phobos meaning “deep dread or aversion”. The degree to which a person suffers from Scopophobia can vary: some are so affected by it that they are afraid of “being watched” all the time. Still others may be Agoraphobic in that; they refuse to step outdoors as they feel they would be stared at by strangers (which makes them want to flee or hide). In either case, the phobics experience a full blown panic attack at the mere thought of being looked at "}}
