{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_309441366#0_541136742","relevance":3,"reason":"Dedicated article on 'Fear of Being Watched Phobia – Scopophobia'; it directly defines scopophobia/scoptophobia as fear of being watched or stared at and explains that sufferers may feel watched all the time or fear strangers staring at them.","learned":"Scopophobia is a specific fear of being watched or stared at; in severe cases people may feel watched all the time, avoid going outdoors, or panic at the thought of being looked at."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3762","reason":"Continue this high-yield scopophobia query to find more dedicated segments on causes and mechanisms of feeling watched or stared at."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3762"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_309441366#2_541140469","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3762","rank":3,"snippet":"as public ridicule for some reason are more likely to develop the fear of being stared at. Others having a physical deformity due to an accident or an illness are naturally more likely to be stared at and could develop the fear over time. People with other social disorders like stage fright, fear of public speaking etc could also develop In general, individuals with low self esteem or those having some self developed body image are likely to suffer from this fear. Naturally, having a small amount of social fear is considered reasonable. However, in extreme Scopophobia, the fear tends to grow out of proportion compared to the actual triggers or risk factors. Autism and Schizophrenia are other existing disorders that are likely to cause the excessive fear of being watched or <cover>stared at. Symptoms of fear of being watched Like other specific and social phobias, Scopophobia </cover>can cause several physical and emotional symptoms in the sufferers. Quiz:\" , \"start_char\": 1192.000000 , \"title\": \"Fear of Being Watched Phobia - Scopophobia\" , \"url\": \"http://www.fearof.net/fear-of-being-watched-phobia-scopophobia/\" }"}}
