{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_309441366#2_541140469","relevance":3,"reason":"Dedicated article on fear of being watched/scopophobia; this segment directly explains causes and risk factors including traumatic public ridicule, visible differences, social fears, low self-esteem, body-image concerns, autism, and schizophrenia.","learned":"Fear of being watched can develop after ridicule or being noticeably stared at, and may be associated with social fears, low self-esteem/body image concerns, autism, or schizophrenia; in scopophobia the fear becomes disproportionate to actual triggers."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3762","reason":"The scopophobia query is yielding dedicated grade-3 evidence about why people feel watched; continue to retrieve additional direct segments or distinct sources."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3762"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_726335721#6_1380114557","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3762","rank":4,"snippet":"afraid that meeting other people will trigger their anxieties. As a consequence of having little or no social contact, these individuals are often more prone to depression. What Causes Scopophobia? Several different conditions can cause scopophobia. Genetics Genetics can play a role in social anxiety, although it is not the most common cause of scopophobia. People with a family history of social anxiety disorder have an increased risk of developing it themselves. Early negative experiences Many phobias, including scopophobia, are triggered by a traumatic experience in early childhood. Studies show that children who have experienced public ridicule, bullying, or abuse are more likely to develop the fear of being stared at later in life. Physical deformity A person with physical deformities caused by illness or injury is more likely to be <cover>stared at and can over time develop the fear of being watched. In general, individuals with low self-esteem due to a negative body image have a heightened risk for scopophobia.</cover>\" , \"start_char\": 3382.000000 , \"title\": \"Scopophobia - Fear of Being Stared At - Practical Psychology\" , \"url\": \"https://practicalpie.com/scopophobia/\" }"}}
