{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_726335721#6_1380114557","relevance":3,"reason":"Dedicated article on scopophobia/fear of being stared at; this segment directly explains causes including genetics/social anxiety risk, early traumatic experiences such as ridicule/bullying/abuse, physical deformity, being stared at, low self-esteem, and negative body image.","learned":"People may feel watched because of scopophobia, which can develop from social anxiety vulnerability, childhood ridicule or bullying, visible physical differences that draw stares, low self-esteem, or negative body image."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3762","reason":"The scopophobia query is yielding distinct dedicated sources with direct causal explanations for feeling watched or stared at; continue to collect high-grade evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3762"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_726335721#7_1380116294","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3762","rank":5,"snippet":"article: \" , \"segment\": \"People with a family history of social anxiety disorder have an increased risk of developing it themselves. Early negative experiences Many phobias, including scopophobia, are triggered by a traumatic experience in early childhood. Studies show that children who have experienced public ridicule, bullying, or abuse are more likely to develop the fear of being stared at later in life. Physical deformity A person with physical deformities caused by illness or injury is more likely to be <cover>stared at and can over time develop the fear of being watched. In general, individuals with low self-esteem due to a negative body image have a heightened risk for scopophobia. </cover>Neurological conditions Some people with epilepsy, schizophrenia, autism spectrum disorders or Tourette’s syndrome can develop scopophobia. They are either afraid that being stared at may trigger an episode or fear that having an episode will cause unwanted attention. How to Manage Scopophobia? If left untreated, scopophobia can worsen over time. In extreme cases, it will have a severe impact on a person's life.\" , \"start_char\": 3797.000000 , \"title\": \"Scopophobia - Fear of "}}
