{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_726335721#7_1380116294","relevance":3,"reason":"Dedicated article on scopophobia/fear of being stared at; this segment directly explains that childhood ridicule, bullying, abuse, physical deformity, low self-esteem, negative body image, and neurological conditions such as epilepsy, schizophrenia, autism, or Tourette's can contribute to fear of being watched.","learned":"Scopophobia-related feelings of being watched may come from traumatic social experiences, body-image or self-esteem concerns, or neurological/developmental/psychiatric conditions where being stared at may trigger or expose symptoms."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3762","reason":"The scopophobia query is still producing dedicated, directly relevant sources about fear of being watched; continue to look for additional distinct grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3762"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_309441366#3_541142322","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3762","rank":6,"snippet":"2953.000000 , \"headings\": \"Fear of Being Watched Phobia – Scopophobia Fear of Being Watched Phobia – Scopophobia Causes of Scopophobia Symptoms of fear of being watched Treating and overcoming Scopophobia \" , \"segment\": \"Naturally, having a small amount of social fear is considered reasonable. However, in extreme Scopophobia, the fear tends to grow out of proportion compared to the actual triggers or risk factors. Autism and Schizophrenia are other existing disorders that are likely to cause the excessive fear of being watched or <cover>stared at. Symptoms of fear of being watched Like other specific and social phobias, Scopophobia </cover>can cause several physical and emotional symptoms in the sufferers. Quiz: Do You Have an Anxiety Disorder? Take the Test Now Most phobics avoid experiencing situations that would render them susceptible to being watched by strangers. They are highly likely to be depressed having little or no social life. Traveling on buses and trains can be traumatic for them. The mere thought of being watched makes them want to flee or hide.\" , \"start_char\": 2112.000000 , \"title\": \"Fear of Being Watched "}}
