{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1689181162#12_2614812616","relevance":3,"reason":"Dedicated mental-health article about paranoia/anxiety over being watched; this segment directly supports that unreasonable fears of surveillance can be linked to schizophrenia or paranoia, and that treatment can help distinguish reasonable monitoring concerns from anxiety or mental-health-driven beliefs.","learned":"Anxiety about being watched may be reasonable in some contexts, but when unreasonable or delusional it can be linked to paranoia or schizophrenia; therapy can help manage the anxiety and separate realistic from unrealistic fears."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3765","reason":"Continue the clinically focused query because it is yielding dedicated mental-health evidence directly explaining feeling watched through paranoia, anxiety, schizophrenia, trauma, and delusional beliefs."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3765"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1340041381#0_2455125956","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3765","rank":3,"snippet":"questions. Please post your question in one of our medical support communities . Stress anxiety and paranoia - how to get out of them frightenedone I think I am suffering from anxiety, or something, and I think its leading to paranoia. I work in a fairly stressful environment, and really don't sleep well. I seldom sleep more than a few hours a night and have been known go go as long as 50 hours at a stretch. Last week I went to the hospital with chest pains. And they have referred me to a doctor. I am worried I will lose my job over this. Its odd, everything I hear somehow makes me feel as though I am <cover>being \"watched\", but I don't know why - that sounds irrational, and quite frankly my own preoccupation makes me worry. Is this paranoia?\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Stress anxiety and paranoia - how to get out of them - Depression/Mental Health - </cover>MedHelp\" , \"url\": \"http://www.medhelp.org/posts/Depression-Mental-Health/Stress-anxiety-and-paranoia---how-to-get-out-of-them/show/329635\" }"}}
