{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"anxiety about being watched\" (+ paranoia delusional schizophrenia treatment))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1689181162#11_2614810810","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3766","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1689181162#11_2614810810\" , \"end_char\": 6511.000000 , \"headings\": \"What Is the Difference Between Paranoia and Reasonable Suspicion? What Is the Difference Between Paranoia and Reasonable Suspicion? What Is Paranoia? Delusional vs. Reasonable Paranoia Schizophrenia Symptoms: The Link to Paranoia and Anxiety When to Seek <cover>Treatment for Anxiety About Being Watched</cover>References: Tonycliftontaxi Jonh Jo \" , \"segment\": \"Trouble with memory, especially working memory. Executive function difficulties that make it difficult to concentrate or stay on task. Trouble starting or sticking with new hobbies or activities. Not talking much. Behavior related to false beliefs. A person with schizophrenia might try to contact a celebrity to warn them of a threat or reach out to a lawyer to report government surveillance that doesn’t seem to be happening. When to Seek Treatment for Anxiety About Being Watched Mental health treatment can help anyone experiencing anxiety, whether their anxiety is rooted in a real source or the product of a mental health diagnosis. Activists such as lawyers or protest leaders who have reasonable fears about being ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1689181162#12_2614812616","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
